HST: Ctrl+Alt+Q starts a new equation, as MathType's key does in Word

Users who come from Word with MathType start an inline equation with Ctrl+Alt+Q. The key was free
in every application. Writer (text and master documents) runs org.hst.office.vi:NewEquation: a new
MathType equation opened in MathType where MathType is installed, else a new formula as the Insert
tab's equation button. Sheets inserts a new empty formula with .uno:InsertObjectStarMath, Slides and
Draw with .uno:InsertMath. The formula opens in the HST Công thức editor (the Math editor with the
template bar and the Elements panel). Menus and ribbon tooltips show the key from the accelerator
configuration as usual.

Test: CppunitTest_sw_hst_equation_shortcut; the MathType choice: tests/unit/test_formula_tools.py (NewEquationTest).

